cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research repository, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Phoenix NPU PQC & QKD: 100% Device-Resident Post-Quantum Cryptography & Quantum Key Distribution on AMD Phoenix NPU"
abstract: "A complete device-resident hardware implementation of the finalized NIST Post-Quantum Cryptography standards (FIPS 202 SHA-3/SHAKE, FIPS 203 ML-KEM, and FIPS 204 ML-DSA) and ETSI GS QKD 014 Quantum Key Distribution (ID Quantique Cerberis XGR compatible) on the AMD Phoenix NPU (Ryzen 7 7840HS / Ryzen 9 7940HS w/ AIE2 / XDNA1 Architecture). Validated across 23 physical silicon gates (839/839 test cases PASS in 35.98s) with zero host CPU cryptographic fallback."
